                                  "value": {
                                    "literal": {
                                      "string": "{0}\n\nIs the departing CEO's immediate successor interim or permanent? A CEO departure is an announced resignation, retirement, removal, death, or other end of service as the filing company's chief executive officer, including an interim or co-CEO, effective now or later. Hypothetical departures, past departures given as background, and departures from other roles or other companies do not count. If several CEOs depart, use the one mentioned first. Use the person who takes over first, even if a permanent successor is also named. Do not infer permanent status from the absence of 'interim'."
